# Window: node rejoin, after the stream snapshot from the live nodes has
#   started arriving. The rejoining node's sites apply each streamed block
#   in StreamSnapshotSink.processMessage.
#
# Fault: on the first block, wait 2 s, then kill the rejoining node's JVM
#   (Runtime.halt, like a power cut: no shutdown hooks). Loaded through the
#   agent's startup script on the rejoining node only, since the rule has to
#   be in place before the rejoin begins.
#
# Correct behaviour: the rejoin fails cleanly; the live nodes stay up and
#   keep serving; a second rejoin without the rule succeeds; no divergence
#   (VoltDB itself crashes on a hash mismatch, and the workload checker
#   checks the data).

RULE rejoin-kill
CLASS org.voltdb.rejoin.StreamSnapshotSink
METHOD processMessage
AT ENTRY
IF $1 != null AND flag("rejoin-kill")
DO traceln("BYTEMAN rejoin-kill fired");
   delay(2000);
   killJVM()
ENDRULE
